  "security_implications": "The txcnt_eq_blksz signal determines when a complete message block has been received for hash processing. If an unsupported digest_size_i is configured (e.g., through a fault injection), txcnt_eq_blksz remains 0 indefinitely, which can stall the HMAC core and lead to a denial-of-service condition. No error alert is generated for this illegal configuration.",
